A||||31||sqoach||Faint "rattle" on acceleration||||9||
Z||000000||sqoach||08-23-2001||07:27 PM||||Not sure what would cause this. Everytime I accelerate, I get this "rattling" sound. I don't know how else to put it. It's not real loud, but noticeable at lower speeds. I'm pretty sure it's coming from the engine. I don't think it's exhaust related. It happens in every gear between 1500 and 2000 RPM. Except on 4th gear. I probably don't hear it if it's there because I'm going too fast. V6 4 spd w/ no cat, if that matters. 82K miles.<BR>Any ideas?<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.gif">   <P>84 SE (FOR SALE)*sale pending*<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)($50)*sale pending*<BR>86 SC (FOR SALE)<BR>86 SE V6 (new project)||||reg||9
Z||000001||Wolfhound||08-23-2001||08:08 PM||||Sqoach, This may or may not relate. My harmonic balancer lost the rubber between the outer ring this week. Rattled on start up and  when I shifted and loud when I cut the engine off. At idle it made a random tick. Otherwise it ran fine. <BR>I like to have never found it.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Mach10||08-23-2001||08:26 PM||||I get a nasty buzzing arcing sound at in-gear-idle. (~1000rpm)<BR>I am reasonably sure that it's a sparkplug that I had dropped in the engine compartment when I had first gotten the car. It never hit the ground, and I haven't ever been able to find it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif"><P>Could it be pinging or knocking? Might be a bad valve/lifter/etc..., OR it could just be shitty gas. Try pouring $5 of premium into an almost empty tank. Does it still do it?<BR>Does it do it out of gear, and free-wheeling?<P>Could be a bad motor mount, bad balancer, loose bolt on a pulley, internal stuff, something knocking on the block, or on the frame. The list goes on... I'd say have someone in the car memorize the noise, then crawl underneath, and start tapping things with a hammer until the volunteer says that the noise is coming from the same area. then see what's loose...<P>Don't know.||||reg||7
Z||000003||Wolfhound||08-23-2001||09:07 PM||||Mach10, I pulled the heat shield off the firewall of a V6, when changing a fuel pump and found three sparkplugs. ||||reg||10
Z||000004||Rick 88||08-24-2001||01:37 AM||||You could be hearing preignition (pinging)<BR>Check your initial timing. If you are running 86 octane regular unleaded this might cause it with the heat. I ran Ed Parks decarbonizer kit in mine and it eliminated the pinging. <P>Rick<BR>yellow 88 GT 5-speed ||||reg||1
Z||000005||rogergarrison||08-24-2001||08:07 AM||||the insides of your catalytic converter? Mine rattles when I start out. oops just noticed you dont have one. never mind.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 08-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||MooCow||08-24-2001||10:32 AM||||Mine was the heat shield that connects where the coil is.  It was missing the bolt and made a rattle noise on take offs.  <P>Thanks Ken<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_7.jpg"> <BR>87 GT, 3.4 engine with a 4:10 tranny, and Viper Yellow!||||reg||1
Z||000007||Songman||08-24-2001||11:22 AM||||I got a wierd rattle like that too, but only when the a/c is on. It is on my 88 T-top coupe with 4 cylinder.. The interior panels are off and this rattle comes right from the panel under the gas tank door release. It is very loud and very annoying. I would think it was just something loose if it didn't just happen with the a/c on. I have no idea.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000008||87GTZ34||08-24-2001||12:52 PM||||Songman, I have the same rattle with a V6. I put insulation and foil tape around the AC lines in an effort to squeeze a few more degrees of cooling from it.  While doing that, I noticed that the junction block that bolts to the frame (just below the driver's behind) is very loose but I haven't had time to see if that is the actual rattle problem.||||reg||1
Z||000009||sqoach||08-24-2001||01:41 PM||||I need to figure out the sound better. It's not really a rattle, but sorta sounds like one. I don't know how to explain it. It doesn't make the noise when I'm out of gear. My car is down for now. Doing brake work. So I can't drive it till I'm finished. I'll bump this topic back up when I figure out some more particulars.||||reg||1
