Z||000012||Mach10||08-24-2001||07:36 PM||||Rattling under load? Is it an Auto or a Manual? If it's Stick, I'd say that you may have a chipped tooth, or a bad bearing.||||reg||7
Z||000013||Songman||08-24-2001||08:14 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MinnGreenGT:<BR><B>songman- is your's a rattle or a squeak?  I get a squeak from that area sometimes, but I'm figuring on a squeaky interior panel- just haven't had time to take it apart.<P>BTW: did you get my email last night?<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Mine is a definite rattle. It sounds like it is in the panel right beside my left ear as I sit in the driver's seat. I can't think of any reason for this to be linked to the a/c since the a/c is on the other side of the car, but it definitely only does it when the a/c is on.. And yeah, I got your e-mail. Just don't have the numbers yet. Everything is boxed and ready to go...<P>Mach, I don't know if your question was for me or someone else but my car is an auto.<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
